<title>UK: Candover invested 27 mln stg in BBC unit buy.</title>
<headline>Candover invested 27 mln stg in BBC unit buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Candover Investments Plc said on Friday it had invested 27 million stg as part of the group that bought the BBC'S domestic radio and television transmission business.</p>
<p>The buy-out specialist made the investment together with the Candover 1994 Fund.</p>
<p>The BBC agreed to sell the business for 244 million stg to Castle Transmission Services, a group that included Candover and was led by Houston-based Castle Tower Corp.</p>
<p>Other partners included Telediffusion de France, part of the France Telecom group Telecom Group and investment firm Berkshire Partners LLC.</p>
<p>The European Commission cleared the acquisition earlier on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
